key_passage.text:
The impulse response of such a filter is $h(t) = \text{sinc} (t/T_s)$ where the **sinc** function is: $$
\text{sinc} (t) = \frac{\sin (\pi t)}{\pi t}
$$ The sinc function is an infinite-length continuous signal that has its maximum at the origin, $\text{sinc} (0)=1$, it is symmetrical, $\text{sinc} (t) = \text{sinc} (-t)$, and it is a sinusoidal wave with a period of 2 that decays in amplitude at a rate $1/t$.

